      "Newcomen's mine pumps, first used in 1712, were important, but they came more than a century earlier and belong to the first industrial revolution, not the steel boom after 1880.",
      "These were textile machines of the 1760s; they show the first industrial revolution, not new ways of making steel.",
      "Electric arc furnaces were only being developed around 1900 and made a small share of steel until well into the twentieth century, so this choice is an anachronism.",
